{"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"Swidux"}],"externalID":"s:6Swidux11EntityStoreVyACyxGSayxGcfc","roleHeading":"Initializer","title":"init(_:)","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"init","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"([","kind":"text"},{"text":"Entity","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"])","kind":"text"}],"symbolKind":"init"},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["macOS"],"tokens":[{"text":"init","kind":"keyword"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"_","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"initialEntities","kind":"internalParam"},{"text":": [","kind":"text"},{"text":"Entity","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"])","kind":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"text":"Discussion","type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"discussion"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Does ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"not","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" record changes — the data is already persisted.","type":"text"}]},{"name":"Important","style":"important","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"This is ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"first-load","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" hydration only. Do not use this initializer","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"to “refresh from disk” mid-session by assigning into a live "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"EntityStore"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"(e.g. ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"state.items = EntityStore(fetched)"},{"text":" from a CloudKit re-hydrate action).","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"In-memory state may hold unflushed writes or live UI bindings; wholesale","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"replacement silently drops them and surfaces as lost keystrokes. Use","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore\/merge(from:shouldReplace:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" for that path — it records no changes and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"lets you decide per-ID which side wins. Under "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"NSPersistentCloudKitContainer"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the gotcha is especially sharp: "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".NSPersistentStoreRemoteChange"},{"type":"text","text":" fires for"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"local saves too, so a naïve “refresh on remote change” observer feeds the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"app its own writes."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"type":"aside"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Entities sharing an ID are collapsed to the first occurrence. A store","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"cannot represent duplicates — ","type":"text"},{"code":"positions","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" holds one index per ID — and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"admitting them corrupts the index: the map would keep only the last","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"index while the array kept every copy, so ","type":"text"},{"code":"count","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" over-reports and a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"later delete orphans the earlier copy with no ","type":"text"},{"code":"positions","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" entry at all,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"leaving a row that is visible in ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore\/values","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" but invisible to","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore\/contains(_:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" and the subscript. Persisted rows can legitimately","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"share an ID (CloudKit forbids unique constraints), so this initializer","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"has to be total rather than trusting its input.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"abstract":[{"text":"Creates a store pre-populated from an array (e.g. first-load hydration at app launch).","type":"text"}],"sections":[],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore"]]},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/swidux\/entitystore\/init(_:)"]}],"kind":"symbol","identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore\/init(_:)"},"references":{"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/EntityStore/values":{"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/entitystore\/values","abstract":[{"text":"All entities in insertion order.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"text":"var","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"values","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": [","kind":"text"},{"text":"Entity","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"]","kind":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore\/values","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","title":"values"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/EntityStore/merge(from:shouldReplace:)":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Merges entities from another store. Entities only present in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"other"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"are always added; for IDs present in both, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"shouldReplace"},{"type":"text","text":" decides"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"whether the incoming value overwrites the one already in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"self"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"merge"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"from"},{"kind":"text","t